# Which graphics driver pack (scripts/build-drivers.sh) a chip needs, by its
# PCI ids as /sys/bus/pci/devices/*/{vendor,device} give them. The first
# line that matches wins; `*` is any device of that vendor. A display
# controller nothing here names gets `software`.
#
# vendor:device   pack

# Intel Gen3 (GMA 900 to 3150): the netbook's chip and its relatives.
8086:2582   gen3
8086:258a   gen3
8086:2592   gen3
8086:2772   gen3
8086:27a2   gen3
8086:27ae   gen3
8086:29b2   gen3
8086:29c2   gen3
8086:29d2   gen3
8086:a001   gen3
8086:a011   gen3
# Every other Intel chip: Gen4 (GMA X3000) to today's.
8086:*      intel

1002:*      amd
10de:*      nvidia

# QEMU's virtio GPU; with 3D off it still has to fall back to software.
1af4:1050   virtual
